+.. _ref_read_monitor_history_example:
+
+Read residual or report-monitor history
+---------------------------------------
+
+**User prompt:**
+
+*"Show the last 50 residual samples from the current Fluent session."*
+
+**Expected tool sequence:**
+
+#. Before the solve, enable the residual plot and initialize the case so
+   PyFluent discovers the monitor set. In Fluent 2025 R2, the plot setting
+   is ``session.settings.solution.monitor.residual.options.plot``.
+#. Call ``read_monitor_history()`` to list monitor sets known to the session.
+#. If the list includes ``residual``, call
+   ``read_monitor_history(monitor_set="residual", max_points=50)`` after the solve.
+#. Use ``x_label`` and ``x_values`` for the horizontal axis. Plot each entry
+   in ``series`` against those values and treat null values as gaps.
+
+PyFluent returns samples captured by its current monitor stream. A session
+that attaches to a running or previously solved case can have partial or
+empty history. Use exactly the set name returned by discovery for a report
+monitor. The response reports ``no_samples`` for an empty set and
+``monitor_set_unavailable`` when the session does not know that set.
+
 Next steps
 ----------
 
